{"acceptedClaimRefs":[{"assessmentDigest":"sha256:ffecb0c1e6dd98e261fe2aee99d428d72719ab6f53a61b37038b6e553b433aef","claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-full-support-necessity","judgmentId":"sha256:571e072efaeb33eb2f5e43a785cda31e611b2a1d4f2c82c7ada68d329c8f41a8","transactionId":"33a5944dca980bf94cc869c6c7dee2d04385ff58"}],"acceptedClaims":[{"claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-full-support-necessity","dependencyTransactionIds":[],"statement":"For the half-skew BSSC product channel P^{otimes 2}, every finite Marton law whose induced super-input X_1X_2 is supported on at most three of {00,01,10,11} has unnormalized Marton sum value strictly below 0.695 bits. A fair one-letter randomized-time-division schedule with reflected rational conditional priors 1/6 and 5/6, repeated independently twice, has exact unnormalized value B_{1/6}=2h_2(1/4)+h_2(1/12)-h_2(5/12)-1/3>0.7231 bits. Therefore every strict two-letter Marton improvement over twice the optimal one-letter randomized-time-division value must assign positive mass to all four super-input symbols. Quantitatively, every such improving witness must assign mass greater than 1/180 to each of 00 and 11 and mass greater than 1/325 to each of 01 and 10. This is a support-pruning theorem for the two-letter Marton functional, not a full-support no-gain theorem or an unrestricted capacity converse."}],"evidenceChunkDigests":["sha256:0df12b3c036fdf29b8c364f0d1c7e0286c2b7d861859a4feb249143a602ec538","sha256:30d12e5f3cb5734207bd2c303528bd247cfc2250e5ab9aabc0e37cf3922bfebd","sha256:757f809dc72142f4b6372c6b764ac553ae290d182c5b40abdca06c8aa85c0522","sha256:9764fcc6d169eaa82f04d483f6dec405c8df5eff3f9c94bcee3dd46a1ee40b69"],"evidenceManifest":{"chunkSizeBytes":65536,"contributionPath":"problems/bssc-sum-capacity/contributions/two-letter-marton-full-support-necessity","files":[{"bytes":11583,"chunks":[{"bytes":11583,"digest":"sha256:30d12e5f3cb5734207bd2c303528bd247cfc2250e5ab9aabc0e37cf3922bfebd","offset":0,"or